          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#statement"} Statement
              %li
                %a{:href => "#proof"} Proof
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            The infinite product formula for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sine"} sine
            function, due to Euler, is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sin
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi n
                        %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sin x = x \prod_{n=1}^\infty (1 - \frac{x^2}{\pi^2 n^2}).
          %p Taking logarithms and then derivatives, this implies the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mi cot
                  %mi π
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %mi n
                    %mo )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \cot \pi x = \frac1{x} + \sum_{n=1}^\infty \left(\frac1{x+n} + \frac1{x-n} \right).
          %p
            Conversely, assuming this cotangent identity, then integrating and exponentiating, we deduce that the product formula is correct up to a constant factor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C = 1
            because
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi sin
                        %mi x
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{x \to 0}{\lim}\; \frac{\sin x}{x} = 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent"} cotangent
          %h2#proof Proof
          %p
            Various proofs of the product formula are known, some relating the product formula to the theory of the Gamma function, some using complex analysis, among others. Below we prove the corresponding identity for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent"} cotangent
            stated above, using an ingenious argument due to Herglotz.
          #OrderOfZero.num_theorem
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mn 0
                    %mi π
                    %mi cot
                    %mi π
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{x \to 0}{\lim} \pi \cot \pi x - \frac1{x} = 0
              \.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p In the right-hand side of the equation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mi cot
                    %mi π
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                        %mi x
                        %mi cos
                        %mi π
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %mi sin
                        %mi π
                        %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mi sin
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mi x
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi \cot \pi x - \frac1{x} = \frac{\pi x\cos \pi x - \sin \pi x}{x \sin{\pi x}},
            %p
              the numerator has a zero of order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
              at
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = 0
          #DoubleAngle.num_theorem
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi π
                    %mi cot
                    %mi π
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = \pi \cot \pi x
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %mn ∞
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo +
                            %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo −
                            %mi n
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) = \frac1{x} + \sum_{n=1}^\infty \left(\frac1{x+n} + \frac1{x-n} \right)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo +
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + f\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right) = 2f(x); \qquad g\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + g\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right) = 2g(x).
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The first follows from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cos
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi sin
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cos\frac{\pi(x+1)}{2} = -\sin\frac{\pi x}{2}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sin
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mi cos
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi π
                          %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sin\frac{\pi(x+1)}{2} = \cos\frac{\pi x}{2}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo −
                          %mi n
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_N(x) = \frac1{x} + \sum_{n=1}^N \left(\frac1{x+n} + \frac1{x-n} \right)
            %p and note that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mi N
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_N\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + g_N\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right) = 2g_{2N}(x) + \frac{2}{x + 2N + 1}.
            %p
              Taking the limit as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \to \infty
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              The function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x) = f(x) - g(x)
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ∖
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R} \setminus \mathbb{Z}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x) = 0
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The oddness and periodicity assertions are obvious, as is continuity at points
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \notin \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{Z}
              follows from Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrderOfZero"}
              and periodicity.
          %p Now we prove the cotangent identity, following the notations of the previous two lemmas:
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By continuity and periodicity,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x)
              attains a maximum value
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo +
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + h\left(\frac{x+1}{2}\right) = 2h(x)
              by Lemma
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleAngle"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\left(\frac{x_0}{2}\right) = M
              follows (else,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                        %mn 2
                      %mo )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\left(\frac{x_0}{2}\right) \lt M
              implies
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mn 0
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                        %mo )
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\left(\frac{x_0+1}{2}\right) \gt M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mi m
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\left(\frac{x_0}{2^m}\right) = M
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mrow
                        %mi m
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mn 2
                            %mi m
                      %mo )
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M = \underset{m \to \infty}{\lim} h\left(\frac{x_0}{2^m}\right) = h(0) = 0.
            %p
              Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi M
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x) \leq M = 0
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x) \leq 0
              and oddness we get that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(x) = 0
              identically, and so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = g(x)
              identically. This completes the proof.
